  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759989,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 18 Years Now - Goldrush's Birthday Demo: A Glimpse into Oceania's Future (C64)\n\nStep into a chillingly familiar world with the *18 Years Now - Goldrush's Birthday Demo*, a playable slice of a Commodore 64 game expanding upon the bleak legacy of George Orwell’s *1984*. Set eighteen years after the novel’s conclusion, this demo offers a brief but unsettling glimpse into Oceania’s continued oppression.\n\nYou play as a nameless citizen, navigating a decaying urban landscape under the ever-watchful gaze of Big Brother. The gameplay focuses on tense, side-scrolling platforming, requiring careful movement and evasion of omnipresent surveillance drones and Thought Police patrols. Collect scattered fragments of forbidden knowledge – snippets of poetry, historical records – to piece together the truth of Oceania’s past and the simmering rebellion brewing beneath the surface.\n\nWhile a short experience, the demo showcases the game's atmospheric visuals, haunting chiptune soundtrack, and the pervasive sense of paranoia that defines life in Oceania. Discover the fate of Winston and Julia, and witness the chilling evolution of the Party's control. This is a demo not just of a game, but of a dystopian"
    },
